Three issues caught on visual review of the merged paper.

Anchor Fig 2 (capability attenuation):
Previous geometry was wrong — AgentA cap and AgentB cap were
positioned so they stuck out past the Root cap on the left,
violating the strict-subset semantics the figure is trying to
convey (and the very invariant listed in its own side panel).
Repositioned with truly nested boxes:
  root  at (0, 0)        spans x in (-4.0, 4.0) y in (-2.8, 2.8)
  mid   at (-0.6, -0.6)  spans x in (-3.5, 2.3) y in (-2.4, 1.2)
  inner at (-1.4, -1.2)  spans x in (-3.0, 0.2) y in (-2.1, 0.3)
inner ⊊ mid ⊊ root holds geometrically. Updated invariants to use
the strict-subset symbol (⊊, not ⊆) and < TTL (not ≤).
